area of high malaria and bacterial infection morbidity &#x0005b;PhD&#x0005d;.</article-title><publisher-loc>Liverpool</publisher-loc><publisher-name>University of Liverpool</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002903-Katz1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Katz</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Chaves</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pellegrino</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1972</year><article-title>A simple device for quantitative stool thick-smear technique in Schistosomiasis mansoni.</article-title><source>Rev Inst Med Trop Sao Paulo</source><volume>14</volume><fpage>397</fpage><lpage>400</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4675644</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002903-Shaker1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shaker</surname><given-names>ZA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hassan</surname><given-names>SI</given-names></name><name><surname>el-Attar</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Talaat</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>el-Nahal</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Use of Kato and nucleopore techniques for qualitative diagnosis of schistosomiasis.</article-title><source>J Egypt Soc Parasitol</source><volume>24</volume><fpage>656</fpage><lpage>662</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7844432</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002903-Molyneux1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Molyneux</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Tembo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kayira</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bwanaisa</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><na